          html: `
<p>Also called management report, operating and financial review, or <b>MD&amp;A</b> (management's discussion and analysis). It is one of the most useful parts of the annual report besides the statements, but apart from figures taken from the statements it is <b>usually unaudited</b> (Germany is an exception: required since 1931 and audited).</p>
<div class="tiles">
  <div class="tile"><h4>IASB Practice Statement – 5 elements</h4><ul><li>Nature of the business</li><li>Management's objectives and strategies</li><li>Significant resources, risks and relationships</li><li>Results of operations</li><li>Critical performance measures</li></ul><p class="small muted">Guidance, not a requirement.</p></div>
  <div class="tile c2"><h4>SEC MD&amp;A – required content</h4><ul><li>Favourable and unfavourable trends; significant events and uncertainties affecting liquidity, capital resources and results</li><li>Effects of inflation and changing prices</li><li>Off-balance-sheet obligations and contractual commitments</li><li>Critical accounting policies needing subjective judgment</li></ul></div>
</div>
<p>Forward-looking parts (planned capex, new stores, divestitures) help with forecasting. But it is management's own view: one input, not an independent opinion.</p>`
